<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 615 0 R/E(Transmitter:)/Alt()/Pg 17 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

242 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 616 0 R/E(The transmitter side includes an Arduino connected to a laser module. The Arduino is programmed to modulate the laser\220s intensity based on binary data \(0s and 1s\), with higher intensity representing a binary \2171\220 and low/off intensity representing a binary \2170\220.)/Alt()/Pg 17 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

243 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 617 0 R/E(Receiver:)/Alt()/Pg 17 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

244 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 618 0 R/E(The receiver circuit uses a photodetector \(a solar panel in this case\) to capture the laser light and convert it back to an electrical signal. This signal is then input to another Arduino that will decode the binary data from the light intensity fluctuations.)/Alt()/Pg 17 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

